    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena multiplied 4.2 by 3.1 and got 130.2.\n\"That cannot be right,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "estimate",
     "decimal places",
     "divisor"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Before multiplying decimals estimate the answer: 4.2 is about 4 and 3.1 is about 3, so the product is about 12. The answer 130.2 is clearly wrong, and the correct answer is 13.02.\nTo multiply, ignore the decimal points, multiply the numbers and then place the decimal so that the answer has as many decimal places as both numbers together.\nTo divide decimals, multiply both numbers by 10 or 100 to make the divisor a whole number."
    }
